{"claims": [{"heading": null, "id": "P:thm:layout", "lean": ["Shape.layout"], "number": "Theorem 1", "paper": "P", "statement": "\\label{thm:layout}\\lean{Shape.layout} Let $E$ be a nonempty type and $1 \\le j \\le k$. For every $x$ there is a constant $C$ such that, for every $n$, both $x \\le C$ and $n + x \\le n + C$.", "status": "linked: Lean proof checked", "status_code": "link.checked", "title": ""}, {"heading": null, "id": "P:thm:witnesses", "lean": ["Shape.witnesses"], "number": "Theorem 2", "paper": "P", "statement": "\\label{thm:witnesses}\\lean{Shape.witnesses} For every $j$ there is a function $x$ with $x(j) = j$ and $j \\le x(j)$, and there is a boolean $x$ that is true.", "status": "linked: Lean proof checked", "status_code": "link.checked", "title": ""}, {"heading": null, "id": "P:thm:shapes", "lean": ["Shape.shapes"], "number": "Theorem 3", "paper": "P", "statement": "\\label{thm:shapes}\\lean{Shape.shapes} Let $E$ be nonempty. No natural number is negative, and either every $n$ satisfies $0 \\le n$ or, if $1 = 1$, some $m$ equals $1$.", "status": "linked: Lean proof checked", "status_code": "link.checked", "title": ""}, {"heading": null, "id": "P:def:multiple", "lean": ["Shape.MultipleAbove", "Shape.fib"], "number": "Definition 1", "paper": "P", "statement": "\\label{def:multiple}\\lean{Shape.MultipleAbove}\\lean{Shape.fib} A number $n$ is a multiple of $m$ above $b$ if $n = mq$ for some $q \\ge b$. The Fibonacci numbers are $F_0 = 0$, $F_1 = 1$ and $F_{n+2} = F_n + F_{n+1}$.", "status": "linked: Lean definition", "status_code": "link.definition", "title": ""}, {"heading": null, "id": "P:thm:supplied", "lean": ["Shape.supplied"], "number": "Theorem 4", "paper": "P", "statement": "\\label{thm:supplied}\\lean{Shape.supplied} Let $s$ be a solution for $d$ with bound at most $5$. Then $s$ starts at most at $5$.", "status": "linked: Lean proof checked", "status_code": "link.checked", "title": ""}, {"heading": null, "id": "P:thm:assumed", "lean": ["Shape.assumed"], "number": "Theorem 5", "paper": "P", "statement": "\\label{thm:assumed}\\lean{Shape.assumed} If every admissible datum has a good solution, then $0$ has a good solution.", "status": "linked: Lean proof checked", "status_code": "link.checked", "title": ""}, {"heading": null, "id": "P:thm:produced", "lean": ["Shape.produced"], "number": "Theorem 6", "paper": "P", "statement": "\\label{thm:produced}\\lean{Shape.produced} Every admissible datum $d$ has a good solution.", "status": "linked: Lean proof checked", "status_code": "link.checked", "title": ""}, {"heading": null, "id": "P:thm:positive", "lean": ["Shape.positive"], "number": "Theorem 7", "paper": "P", "statement": "\\label{thm:positive}\\lean{Shape.positive} Every positive number is at least $1$.", "status": "linked: Lean proof checked", "status_code": "link.checked", "title": ""}, {"heading": null, "id": "P:thm:single", "lean": ["Shape.single"], "number": "Theorem 8", "paper": "P", "statement": "\\label{thm:single}\\lean{Shape.single} A type with a single element has at most one element, and exactly one.", "status": "linked: Lean proof checked", "status_code": "link.checked", "title": ""}, {"heading": null, "id": "P:thm:probability", "lean": ["Shape.probability"], "number": "Theorem 9", "paper": "P", "statement": "\\label{thm:probability}\\lean{Shape.probability} On a probability space, the whole space has measure one.", "status": "linked: Lean proof checked", "status_code": "link.checked", "title": ""}, {"heading": null, "id": "P:thm:none-large", "lean": ["Shape.none_large"], "number": "Theorem 10", "paper": "P", "statement": "\\label{thm:none-large}\\lean{Shape.none_large} No solution for $0$ has a negative bound.", "status": "linked: Lean proof checked", "status_code": "link.checked", "title": ""}, {"heading": null, "id": "P:thm:two-solutions", "lean": ["Shape.two_solutions"], "number": "Theorem 11", "paper": "P", "statement": "\\label{thm:two-solutions}\\lean{Shape.two_solutions} Two solutions $s$ and $t$ for the same datum start at the same point.", "status": "linked: Lean proof checked", "status_code": "link.checked", "title": ""}, {"heading": null, "id": "P:thm:both", "lean": ["Shape.both"], "number": "Theorem 12", "paper": "P", "statement": "\\label{thm:both}\\lean{Shape.both} If $a \\le b$ and $b \\le a$, then $a = b$.", "status": "linked: Lean proof checked", "status_code": "link.checked", "title": ""}, {"heading": null, "id": "P:def:profile", "lean": ["Shape.Profile", "Shape.Concrete"], "number": "Definition 2", "paper": "P", "statement": "\\label{def:profile}\\lean{Shape.Profile}\\lean{Shape.Concrete} A profile is a function $f$ with $f(n) \\le C$ for every $n$. A concrete profile is a profile that vanishes from $N$ on and has period $p$ below $N$.", "status": "linked: Lean definition", "status_code": "link.definition", "title": ""}, {"heading": null, "id": "P:thm:build", "lean": ["Shape.build", "Shape.build_rec"], "number": "Theorem 13", "paper": "P", "statement": "\\label{thm:build}\\lean{Shape.build}\\lean{Shape.build_rec} The zero profile below $N$ is a concrete profile, and $f(n + 1) = f(n)$ for it.", "status": "linked: Lean definition", "status_code": "link.definition", "title": ""}, {"heading": null, "id": "P:thm:vanishes", "lean": ["Shape.vanishes"], "number": "Theorem 14", "paper": "P", "statement": "\\label{thm:vanishes}\\lean{Shape.vanishes} A concrete profile vanishes from $N$ on.", "status": "linked: Lean proof checked", "status_code": "link.checked", "title": ""}, {"heading": null, "id": "P:thm:scaled", "lean": ["Shape.scaled"], "number": "Theorem 15", "paper": "P", "statement": "\\label{thm:scaled}\\lean{Shape.scaled} A scaled family for $d$ and $w$ that starts at $d$ starts at $d$.", "status": "linked: Lean proof checked", "status_code": "link.checked", "title": ""}, {"heading": null, "id": "P:thm:both-pos", "lean": ["Shape.both_pos"], "number": "Theorem 16", "paper": "P", "statement": "\\label{thm:both-pos}\\lean{Shape.both_pos} An object with both extents has a positive first coordinate.", "status": "linked: Lean proof checked", "status_code": "link.checked", "title": ""}, {"heading": null, "id": "P:thm:jet", "lean": ["Shape.jet_lower"], "number": "Theorem 17", "paper": "P", "statement": "\\label{thm:jet}\\lean{Shape.jet_lower} If the first $n + 5$ differences of $f$ are bounded by $C$ on $S$, so are the first $n + 4$.", "status": "linked: Lean proof checked", "status_code": "link.checked", "title": ""}, {"heading": null, "id": "P:thm:below", "lean": ["Shape.below_succ", "Shape.every_below"], "number": "Theorem 18", "paper": "P", "statement": "\\label{thm:below}\\lean{Shape.below_succ}\\lean{Shape.every_below} A vector bounded by $i$ is bounded by $i + 1$; vectors bounded by $7$ are bounded by $8$.", "status": "linked: Lean proof checked", "status_code": "link.checked", "title": ""}, {"heading": null, "id": "P:thm:steps", "lean": ["Shape.steps_pos", "Shape.pick_at"], "number": "Theorem 19", "paper": "P", "statement": "\\label{thm:steps}\\lean{Shape.steps_pos}\\lean{Shape.pick_at} The number of steps down from $k + 3$ is positive, and $\\mathrm{pick}(k + 1, 0) = 1$.", "status": "linked: Lean proof checked", "status_code": "link.checked", "title": ""}, {"heading": null, "id": "P:thm:conditional", "lean": ["Shape.conditional"], "number": "Theorem 20", "paper": "P", "statement": "\\label{thm:conditional}\\lean{Shape.conditional} If every $x$ with $A(x)$ has some $y$ with $B(x, y)$, and $A(a)$ holds, then some $y$ has $B(a, y)$.", "status": "linked: Lean proof checked", "status_code": "link.checked", "title": ""}, {"heading": null, "id": "P:thm:alternating", "lean": ["Shape.alternating"], "number": "Theorem 21", "paper": "P", "statement": "\\label{thm:alternating}\\lean{Shape.alternating} For every $x$ there is $y$ such that $x + z \\le y + z$ for every $z$.", "status": "linked: Lean proof checked", "status_code": "link.checked", "title": ""}, {"heading": null, "id": "P:thm:premised", "lean": ["Sh